<style>
	/*
	 * The suggested words.
	 *
	 * A list rather than comma-joined inline text, for one concrete reason: the obvious
	 * `{i > 0 && ", "}` separator renders here as "Logos , Games , Motion / Video .",
	 * because Astro keeps the whitespace between two JSX expressions where JSX would
	 * strip it. A separator written in markup is a separator you then have to fight.
	 *
	 * A list of short words needs no separator at all — the gap reads as the list — and
	 * the middot is a pseudo-element, so nothing in the markup can leave a stray space
	 * beside it. The tap floor is kept because these are real links, not decoration.
	 */
	.words {
		display: inline;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
